{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":40.65999984741211,"text":"The town's football ground is named after a real person. Diogoras of Rhodes was a boxer and won at Olympia in 464 B.C. He is not remembered for his own victory, though. He is remembered because his children won, too. At one festival at Olympia, two of his sons were crowned on the same day, and the moment their contests ended, they lifted him onto their shoulders and carried him around the stadium while the crowd threw flowers. Somebody in the stands shouted that there was nothing left for him to wish for. Diogoras died that same day, there in his son's arms, and the story traveled for centuries as an example of the happiest moment a person can have.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.5400000214576721},{"word":"town's","start":0.5400000214576721,"end":1.0800000429153442},{"word":"football","start":1.0800000429153442,"end":1.340000033378601},{"word":"ground","start":1.340000033378601,"end":1.6200000047683716},{"word":"is","start":1.6200000047683716,"end":2.0199999809265137},{"word":"named","start":2.0199999809265137,"end":2.059999942779541},{"word":"after","start":2.059999942779541,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"a","start":2.359999895095825,"end":2.680000066757202},{"word":"real","start":2.680000066757202,"end":2.880000114440918},{"word":"person","start":2.880000114440918,"end":3.319999933242798},{"word":"Diogoras","start":4.179999828338623,"end":4.420000076293945},{"word":"of","start":4.420000076293945,"end":4.820000171661377},{"word":"Rhodes","start":4.820000171661377,"end":5.139999866485596},{"word":"was","start":5.139999866485596,"end":5.400000095367432},{"word":"a","start":5.400000095367432,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"boxer","start":5.900000095367432,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"and","start":5.900000095367432,"end":6.260000228881836},{"word":"won","start":6.260000228881836,"end":6.420000076293945},{"word":"at","start":6.420000076293945,"end":6.739999771118164},{"wo